WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.830
So I want to spend just a few minutes talking
about the November 2020 election, but the

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:09.220
context is really going to be coronavirus
because there's a very interesting new study

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:14.380
which found that if you break down Donald
Trump's approval rating in counties where

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:20.820
Corona virus is raging versus in counties
where it is not, this is a county level analysis.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:26.330
Counties that are seeing the highest rates
of corona virus explosion have seen a dramatic

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.730
drop in Donald Trump's approval rating.

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:33.190
And the reason this is important is that last
week I did a segment pointing out that, you

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:37.340
know, when we think about the Biden versus
Trump debates, assuming that they happen,

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:41.790
Biden pointing out that Trump is crass and
makes fun of people and is a bully and grab

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:45.450
them by the You-Know-What and the racism and
xenophobia and all that stuff.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:46.850
It hasn't worked so far.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:50.190
And I can't imagine that it's going to all
of a sudden start working for Joe Biden if

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.410
that's the approach he decides to take.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:57.780
My instinct was we've seen Trump's approval
come down because of three major issues over

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.050
the last four months.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:01.309
Number one, the handling of Corona virus.

00:01:01.309 --> 00:01:06.140
Number two, the handling of the economy in
the context of the failed handling of corona

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:07.140
virus.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:12.630
And number three, the insane reaction to protests
against police brutality, which included authoritarian

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:19.249
anti speech tendencies and threats to send
in troops with even more force to protests

00:01:19.249 --> 00:01:21.759
that are against police brutality to begin
with.

00:01:21.759 --> 00:01:27.159
That's where the focus should be and particularly
the failure of leadership.

00:01:27.159 --> 00:01:32.179
Language aside, if Trump uses coarse language
but he crushes the virus and does the right

00:01:32.179 --> 00:01:34.569
thing when it comes to protests and the economy.

00:01:34.569 --> 00:01:37.219
OK, who's going to care about the coarse language?

00:01:37.219 --> 00:01:38.820
And that's basically my idea.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:44.750
And indeed, Donald Trump has seen the fastest
declines in his approval rating in the 500

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:50.749
counties where there have been more than 28
corona virus deaths per 100000 residents.

00:01:50.749 --> 00:01:52.670
That's sort of like the dividing line.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:02:00.619
Pew Research Polling shows that 17 percent
of the country which approved of Trump in

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:02.889
March now disapprove.

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:05.899
So it's starting with just the slice that
approved in March.

00:02:05.899 --> 00:02:09.179
17 percent of that now disapproves.

00:02:09.179 --> 00:02:14.769
And this is a in those counties and this is
a massive drop and we're not even near the

00:02:14.769 --> 00:02:16.319
end of the pandemic.

00:02:16.319 --> 00:02:17.409
And.

00:02:17.409 --> 00:02:25.780
It's always tragic when it takes friends or
family members getting sick or dying to wake

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:32.260
up and have a realization, it's like the anti-gay
Republican politician who changes their tune.

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:37.280
Typically his tune, but their tune when someone
they know comes out as gay.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:38.280
Great.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:39.569
They came to the right conclusion.

00:02:39.569 --> 00:02:42.099
But why did it take that you couldn't empathize?

00:02:42.099 --> 00:02:45.510
Well, it seems like that's at least part of
what's going on here.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:51.609
And there's a very reasonable debate over
how much is Trump's fault in terms of the

00:02:51.609 --> 00:02:53.280
cases and deaths.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.790
Obviously, people were going to die.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:58.980
You can't say of one hundred and thirty two
thousand deaths.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:00.829
One hundred and thirty two thousand.

00:03:00.829 --> 00:03:01.959
Are Trump's fault.

00:03:01.959 --> 00:03:06.989
But you can put numbers on what was the cost
of not developing a testing program starting

00:03:06.989 --> 00:03:12.050
January 20th, the way South Korea did when
we both got our first cases on the same day.

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:19.879
You can make estimates about what would a
mask recommendation have done early on?

00:03:19.879 --> 00:03:22.530
What would stay at home have done early on?

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:26.079
Hospitals could have maybe not been underwhelm
like, you know, overwhelmed.

00:03:26.079 --> 00:03:27.540
You can put numbers to this.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.400
And so, you know, people who want to argue
Trump doesn't have one hundred and thirty

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.549
two thousand deaths on his hands, of course
he doesn't.

00:03:33.549 --> 00:03:36.340
I don't know anyone who's actually making
that case.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:41.129
What we know is that there are specific policies
and specific actions, including the rollout

00:03:41.129 --> 00:03:46.099
of the testing program and many other things
that could have been done differently, which

00:03:46.099 --> 00:03:47.470
would have saved lives.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:49.010
And it's not could have been done differently.

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:50.060
But nobody did that.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:51.069
Many countries did.

00:03:51.069 --> 00:03:52.489
South Korea is an example.

00:03:52.489 --> 00:03:53.739
There are many others.

00:03:53.739 --> 00:03:59.150
Remember that on February 26, Donald Trump
said we have 15 cases and 15 is soon going

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:00.150
to zero.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:01.890
That was February 26.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:06.290
We now have almost three million cases and
one hundred and thirty two thousand deaths

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:10.769
and cases are exploding in a huge swath of
this country.

00:04:10.769 --> 00:04:13.219
So that's the context.

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:19.449
And it is, again, evidence that the pandemic
and Trump's reaction are dramatically hurting

00:04:19.449 --> 00:04:20.449
his polling.

00:04:20.449 --> 00:04:24.009
Now, to zoom out a little bit bigger picture,
we continue to get national polling where

00:04:24.009 --> 00:04:26.380
Trump is down by double digits.

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:31.770
We also are seeing real clear politics polling
averages in Wisconsin, Michigan, Pennsylvania

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:35.650
and Florida, where Biden is ahead by five
or more points.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:37.090
That's insane.

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:40.110
Arizona, which has been a Republican stronghold
for a long time.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:43.080
Biden ahead by an average of three and a half
and a half.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:48.650
The really crazy thing to think about is that
if Donald Trump had just taken medical advice

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:53.520
and gone the route of other countries that
chose chose science over ignorance and action

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.199
over politics.

00:04:55.199 --> 00:05:00.419
If he had controlled the corona virus and
supported a shutdown, supported of an actual

00:05:00.419 --> 00:05:06.030
real testing program starting in January,
tracing initiatives, et cetera, et cetera,

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:08.870
he would have an all but guaranteed reelection
in November.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:13.600
I am increasingly confident that that is that
that that is how important this is ultimately

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:15.169
going to be.

00:05:15.169 --> 00:05:20.030
And it's also crazy to think that if Trump
and Pence had just caught the flu or a bad

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:25.150
intestinal bug on January 20th and been MEAA
for a month and just let medical doctors make

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:27.669
decisions, we would also be far better off.

00:05:27.669 --> 00:05:32.480
In other words, their presence was not only
not positive, it was acutely negative in dealing

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:33.960
with coronavirus.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:35.710
The data is in the polls.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:39.260
And so what do we all have to do now?

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:40.260
Exactly.

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:44.069
We don't believe any one of the polls, we
imagine that our individual votes could be

00:05:44.069 --> 00:05:50.570
the difference makers in our states and every
single one of us gets an absentee ballot or

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:55.560
goes in votes or does whatever it is that
we can do to ensure that Donald Trump is removed

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:56.560
in November.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:57.560
The polling looks good.

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:58.560
Ignore it.

00:05:58.560 --> 00:05:59.680
Pretend the polling looks terrible.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:01.800
Pretend every state is 50/50.

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:03.270
And that you could be the difference maker.

